            <ArticleTitle>[Rheoencephalography in headache paroxysms of vascular origin and several therapeutic problems].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>377-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author conducted a REG study of 68 patients who were referred to hospitals due to paroxysmal headaches of a vascular genesis. Changes characteristic of attacks of headaches with phasic cerebral disturbances were revealed. The results of such studies were used for prescribing rational therapy and for the assessment of the working capacity of these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
